# Cloudflare Pages response headers.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ models
# 16.1 MB across two files, previously served as `max-age=0, must-revalidate`.
# The bytes were spared on a 304, but only while the browser still held them —
# and unhashed multi-megabyte files are the first thing a phone evicts, so
# repeat visitors were re-downloading them. Every visit also paid two
# revalidation round-trips before inference could start.
#
# These filenames are content-stable: the vector contract pins the exact model
# revision, so det_500m.onnx and w600k_mbf.onnx cannot change meaning without
# the whole index being rebuilt. That makes them safe to freeze.
#
# IF A MODEL IS EVER SWAPPED, RENAME THE FILE. Editing one in place would leave
# clients on a year-old copy, producing embeddings that silently disagree with
# the index — the exact failure tools/golden exists to catch.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Vite fingerprints everything in /assets, so these are safe to freeze too.
# Includes the 12.9 MB onnxruntime wasm binary.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# ----------------------------------------------- why there is no COOP/COEP
# face.ts asks onnxruntime for up to 4 wasm threads whenever
# `self.crossOriginIsolated` is true, which needs:
#
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
#   Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
#
# That was implemented and then backed out, because turning it on breaks face
# search. Measured 2026-08-10 with both headers set: `crossOriginIsolated` went
# true, ORT switched to its multithreaded path, and
# `InferenceSession.create()` never settled — no error, no rejection, and the
# model files were never requested. The search sat on "Searching…" forever.
# Pinning numThreads to 1 with the same headers loaded both models instantly.
#
# The groundwork is done and is safe to leave in place, so a future attempt is
# a small change rather than a risky one:
#   - the Worker sends `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin` on /r2/*
#   - public asset URLs carry ?v=N (apps/api/src/lib.ts), so a browser holding
#     a year-old `immutable` copy without CORP re-fetches instead of showing a
#     broken photo
#
# To retry: remove the numThreads pin in face.ts, add the two headers here and
# to `server.headers` in vite.config.ts, and verify an END-TO-END search
# returns photos on a real phone. `crossOriginIsolated === true` is not
# evidence that it works — that was true the whole time it was hanging.
